  "POST /api/v1/aito/{project_id}/invoice": {
   "description": "Raise the invoice for a finished project, paid down by its deposits.\n\nZOHO-FIRST, like ``send_invoice_email``: the invoice IS the act, and\nnothing is written locally until Books confirms it exists. A timeline\nentry for an invoice that was never raised is worse than none.\n\nThe plan is re-read here rather than taken from the preview the dialog\nshowed, for the same reason the send route re-reads its recipients: what\nthe client echoes back is not evidence. That costs one extra estimate\nread and buys the guarantee that the lines billed are the lines Books\nholds at the moment of billing.\n\nThe retainer application deliberately cannot fail this request. Once\n``create_invoice`` returns, a real document exists in the client's\naccount; a 500 after that point would invite a retry that raises a\nSECOND one. So ``apply_retainers`` swallows its own upstream errors and\nreports what it managed, and the response says which deposits landed.\n\nOne consequence worth naming: the new invoice makes\n``aito_quote_sync._is_locked`` true (non-empty ``invoice_ids``), so the\nquote stops accepting line edits from this app on the next sync pass.\nThat is the existing, intended rule \u2014 an invoiced estimate is accounting,\nnot a draft \u2014 and it is why the confirm dialog exists.",
   "operationId": "create_invoice_api_v1_aito__project_id__invoice_post",
   "parameters": [
    {
     "in": "path",
     "name": "project_id",
     "required": true,
     "schema": {
      "title": "Project Id",
      "type": "integer"
     }
    },
    {
     "in": "header",
     "name": "X-API-Key",
     "required": false,
     "schema": {
      "anyOf": [
       {
        "type": "string"
       },
       {
        "type": "null"
       }
      ],
      "title": "X-Api-Key"
     }
    }
   ],
   "responses": {
    "200": {
     "content": {
      "application/json": {
       "schema": {
        "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AitoInvoiceCreatedResponse"
       }
      }
     },
     "description": "Successful Response"
    },
    "422": {
     "content": {
      "application/json": {
       "schema": {
        "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
       }
      }
     },
     "description": "Validation Error"
    }
   },
   "security": [
    {
     "HTTPBearer": []
    }
   ],
   "summary": "Create Invoice",
   "tags": [
    "aito"
   ]
  },
