  "POST /api/v1/aito/{project_id}/tracking-token": {
   "description": "Kill a leaked link: a new token, the old one 404s at once. The event\ncarries no token \u2014 the log is readable by every aito:read holder, and\nsince T-015 board responses do not carry the link either: the URL is\nserved only by the two AITO_UPDATE routes here, both no-store.\n\nThe new token is committed BEFORE Books is contacted. Two reasons: the\nleaked link must die whatever Books does next, and the row must not sit\ndirty across the HTTP round trips \u2014 the first settings read inside the\nZoho client would autoflush it and hold SQLite's write lock for up to\ntwo request timeouts, longer than the busy timeout, so unrelated writers\n(MQTT status, the sync worker) failed with \"database is locked\".\n\nThe old link is printed on the quote too, so the estimate's notes are\nrewritten here and now rather than at the next line sync, which may be\ndays away. Books being unreachable never blocks the local change, but\nthe response says so, and the next sync rewrites the notes anyway\n(notes_with_tracking sees the stale block).",
   "operationId": "regenerate_tracking_token_api_v1_aito__project_id__tracking_token_post",
   "parameters": [
    {
     "in": "path",
     "name": "project_id",
     "required": true,
     "schema": {
      "title": "Project Id",
      "type": "integer"
     }
    },
    {
     "in": "header",
     "name": "X-API-Key",
     "required": false,
